  "question": {
    "text": "A pole stands vertically inside a triangular park&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>. Let the angle of elevation of the top of&nbsp;the pole from each corner of the park be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>.&nbsp;If the radius of the circumcircle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>,&nbsp;then the height of the pole is equal to :<gwmw style=\"display:none;\"></gwmw>"
  },
